WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.920
Vitamin B12 supplementation is crucial
for anyone eating a plant-based diet,

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:07.740
but does it have any side effects?

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.660
Watch the video to find out.

00:00:09.814 --> 00:00:16.211
"Do Vitamin B12 Supplements Cause
Acne, Bone Fractures, and Lung Cancer?"

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:23.700
Acne is a disease unique to humans.
Why do humans get acne?

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:31.140
Well, think about the distribution of those greasy
sebaceous glands—face, chest and back—

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:34.140
exactly the same structures
that pose the greatest

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:37.980
obstruction during childbirth.
So hey, maybe having a little

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:41.580
extra lubrication at those sites
would help make the baby

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:44.580
more slippery for birth,
conferring a selective advantage

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:48.840
for successful delivery.
OK, but what triggers them

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:55.080
to become inflamed into zits later on?
While in westernized societies, acne

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:59.940
is a nearly universal skin disease
afflicting up to 95% of teens,

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:03.360
in some populations eating
more traditional diets not even

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:07.620
single cases could be found.
This suggests that perhaps

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:10.920
nutrition counseling should be
a first-line therapy for individuals

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:16.260
with mild to moderate acne.
It looks like it's the high glycemic

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:20.760
foods and dairy products.
So we're talking sugar, soda,

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:25.200
refined junky carbs, white flour,
breakfast cereal, and dairy products

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:29.880
like milk, cheese, yogurt, whey,
as well as saturated and trans fats

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:33.300
concentrated in meat,
dairy, junk, and fast food.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:38.340
So for example, acne patients should
be encouraged to discontinue

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:40.440
any whey protein supplements
they might be taking.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:44.940
The relationship between milk and
acne severity may be explained

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:50.100
by the presence in dairy of normal
reproductive sex steroid hormones

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:54.420
or the enhanced production of
growth hormones such as IGF-1.

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:59.160
And if you re like, "Wait, I gave up
dairy a month ago and still no change,"

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:03.240
It should be noted that changes
in acne due to any dietary changes

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:08.340
are likely to take at least 10 to 12
weeks, so you have to stick to it.

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:12.600
Not surprisingly, acne patients
were more than twice as likely

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:15.720
to have a non-vegan diet
compared to controls,

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:19.260
but the difference did not
reach statistical significance.

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:22.320
So maybe the vegans were
eating a lot of vegan junk?

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:29.100
But what about this:
"Vitamin B12 Induced Acnes"

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:34.380
Our fellow great ape herbivores like
gorillas get all the B12 they need

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:39.000
practicing the eating of feces,
but my preference would be

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:43.140
to take B12 supplements.
And you don't have to worry

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:46.500
about getting too much because
there are evidently no reports

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:49.680
of adverse effects associated
with excess B12 intake,

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:52.080
but that's not true.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:58.620
First described back in the 1950's,
about 1 in 10 people erupt in acne

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:04.200
within days or even just within hours
of getting an injection of vitamin B12,

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.900
which then disappears rapidly
when you stop injecting them.

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:10.140
At the time, we had no idea
what the mechanism might be,

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:14.100
a problem still unsolved even
up until just to a few years ago.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:18.420
But then we finally figured it out:
Vitamin B12 modulates

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:21.540
the gene expression of the skin
bacteria that cause acne.

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:24.780
They swabbed the skin of 10 people
before and after being injected

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:28.200
with Vitamin B12. It turns out
the level of B12 on your skin

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:31.920
is proportional to the level in
your blood, and so after injection

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:35.760
the bacteria on your skin have
to make less of their own B12,

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:39.180
and so the acne bacteria could
concentrate instead on using

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:43.380
its cellular machinery to churn out
more compounds to attack your face.

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:47.040
Without excess B12 on the skin,
shown here in green,

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:54.600
the bacteria has to make most on
its own at the expense of porphyrins,

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:59.160
which can trigger acne inflammation.
When there's lots of B12 floating around,

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:04.380
the bacteria can not waste resources
and focus instead on trying to pimple

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:10.740
you up. OK, so wait, what do you do?
Those on plant-based diets have

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:15.900
to take supplemental B12. Yes,
but we don't have to get injections.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:20.940
Vitamin B12-related acne tends to
occur only in dosages in excess of

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:26.580
5,000 to 10,000 micrograms a week,
well in excess of the 50 micrograms

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:29.220
a day I recommend, or
alternately my 2,000

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:31.980
single weekly dose. I mean
the only time you'd be taking

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:37.440
between 5,000 to 10,000 a week
is if you were treating B12 deficiency.

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:40.860
If you remember from my previous
video, B12 deficiency is treated with

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:43.800
1,000 micrograms a day
for a month or more,

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:48.360
and that could potentially trigger it,
as noted in this vegan woman

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:51.240
who wasn't taking B12,
developed B12 deficiency,

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:55.860
and had to be treated with such high
doses her face erupted in acne.

00:04:55.860 --> 00:05:00.060
So all the more reason not to fall
B12 deficient in the first place.

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:04.860
But look, if worse comes to worst,
even if you do get B12 injections,

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:10.080
the likelihood of it triggering
acne may only be about 1 in 10.

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:14.700
In 2019, a study found an
“Association Between

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:18.780
High Intakes of Vitamins B6 and B12
From Food and Supplements With

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:21.720
(the) Risk of Hip Fracture Among
Postmenopausal Women

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:23.640
in the Harvard Nurses’ Health Study.”

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:27.480
But note, it was only
the combined high intake

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:29.040
of vitamins B6 and B12.

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:31.920
We know that treatment with
high doses of vitamin B6

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:34.380
may alone increase hip fracture risk.

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:37.500
After a decade or so,
those who had been taking

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:41.700
high dose B6 supplements had about
a 40% higher hip fracture risk,

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:44.760
but not in those taking B12.

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:47.160
And that’s what the
Harvard study found too—

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:48.840
high intake of vitamin B12 alone

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:51.420
was not associated with increased risk.

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:54.000
In fact, some observational
studies suggest slightly

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:57.480
lower fracture risk at
high B12 blood levels.

00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:01.620
But what we care about most
are interventional studies,

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:05.340
where people are randomized to
B12 so we can see what happens.

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:09.480
And when you do that,
no increased fracture risk

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:11.040
among those given B12.

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:14.640
In conclusion, based on
randomized controlled trials,

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:17.880
high doses of vitamin
B12 have not been shown

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:20.940
to be associated with
the risk of fractures.

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:23.520
OK, but what about this?

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:28.860
In 2017, a study found that men
taking vitamin B12 supplements

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:32.220
appeared to have an increase
in lung cancer risk.

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:35.100
Now, they didn’t find any
such association in women,

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:37.200
and it was mostly among smoking men.

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:41.280
Could it be that B12 was like
feeding some budding tumors?

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:44.460
I mean, it’s hard to imagine
a vitamin being carcinogenic

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:48.420
on its own, and especially somehow
only in men but not women.

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:51.780
The bottom line is that
replication of these ﬁndings

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:53.460
with additional studies is necessary,

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:56.760
and indeed when you put all the
observational studies together,

00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:59.880
there was no signiﬁcant correlation
between the levels of B12

00:06:59.880 --> 00:07:03.180
in the blood and lung cancer,
whether you smoked or not.

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:05.700
If anything, most studies
seemed to be trending

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:08.820
towards higher B12 levels
being protective.

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:12.780
But then, in 2018, a new study
found an association

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:15.120
between overall lung cancer
risk and higher

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:16.740
circulating levels of B12,

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:19.500
again appearing to be
more of a smoker thing.

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:21.960
Now, this was another
observational study.

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:25.440
Those with higher B12
levels were just observed

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:27.240
to have higher cancer levels;

00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:31.500
and so, those of you who have been
following my work know the drill.

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:33.600
There are two potential issues that arise

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:36.480
in observational studies that
prevent you from ascribing

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:39.600
cause-and-effect: confounding
factors, also known as

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:42.060
“lurking variables” and
reverse causation.

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:46.260
What might be a lurking variable
in this case, a third factor

00:07:46.260 --> 00:07:49.260
associated with both higher
B12 levels and cancer,

00:07:49.260 --> 00:07:50.820
that may be the true cause?

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:54.600
Well, who has higher levels of B12
circulating in their blood?

00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:57.660
Those who eat lots of meat and dairy,

00:07:57.660 --> 00:08:00.420
in fact probably the most
important contributors.

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:03.600
And those who eat more meat do
tend to have more lung cancer,

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:08.460
about 35% more risk for every
about daily quarter-pound burger,

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:12.360
and 20% increased risk for each
like, breakfast sausage link.

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:16.140
So, no wonder those with higher
B12 levels in their blood

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:17.760
could have more lung cancer.

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:21.000
The B12 could just be a
marker for meat intake.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:24.060
And, if you remember,
reverse causation is when

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:28.320
instead of X leading to Y,
maybe Y is instead leading to X.

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:32.940
So, instead of high B12 blood
levels leading to cancer,

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:35.640
maybe cancer leads to high blood levels.

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:38.280
And indeed, nearly three-quarters
of cancer patients

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:40.920
exhibit elevated B12 levels.

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:44.700
So, elevated B12 levels may
just be a marker for cancer.

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:48.300
There are all sorts of things
beyond just taking extra B12

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:51.000
that can raise your levels:
liver problems, kidney problems,

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:53.160
bone marrow problems, and cancer.

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:56.340
So, high levels may just
be a marker of a brewing,

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:58.440
not-yet-diagnosed, cancer.

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:01.680
Yeah, but what about
observational studies

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:05.040
specifically linking supplement
use to lung cancer?

00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:08.280
That too could be reverse causation,

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:10.500
where being at risk for
cancer—in other words,

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:13.800
being a smoker—makes you
more likely to take vitamins

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:15.480
to try to decrease your risk.

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:19.920
Basically, any behavior tied to
smoking could be indirectly tied

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:22.980
to lung cancer, but it’s
the smoking itself, of course,

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:24.960
that’s the real lung cancer risk.

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:29.100
So, we’re left with this chicken
or the egg causality dilemma,

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:33.960
which is why ideally, we need
randomized controlled trials

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:36.060
to see if there’s any cause-and-effect.

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:39.240
This became even more urgent
with genetic evidence

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:42.240
suggesting that those just
born with higher lifelong levels

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:43.680
may be at increased risk.

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:46.380
Thankfully we do have
randomized controlled trials—

00:09:46.380 --> 00:09:48.720
over a dozen randomized
controlled trials

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:52.800
randomizing thousands of people
up to 2,000 micrograms of B12

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:54.600
every single day for years and…

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:59.160
vitamin B supplementation does not
have any effect on getting cancer,

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:01.470
dying from cancer, or dying overall,

00:10:01.470 --> 00:10:04.560
and this includes specifically
looking at lung cancer.

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:07.800
In fact, if anything, vitamin B
supplements may actually lower

00:10:07.800 --> 00:10:11.347
the risk of the most
dangerous form of skin cancer.

